<title>TUNISIA: Tunisian ex-Hyatt, Club Med hotel to be sold.</title>
<headline>Tunisian ex-Hyatt, Club Med hotel to be sold.</headline>
<dateline>TUNIS 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Compagnie Touristique Arabe (CTA) on Monday said it has launched an international tender to sell off a five-star hotel which was previously run by Hyatt Regency and by Club Med.</p>
<p>It said the 400-bed Hotel Regency, in the Tunisian resort of Monastir, was build in 1985 and was part of a tourist complex it owns in Monastir including a marina.</p>
<p>CTA, a privately-owned company, has capital of 15 million dinars. ($=0.97 dinar)</p>
